  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  tag: v40r4\n  version: ${{ tag[1:] | replace('r', '.') | replace('p', '.') }}\n\npackage:\n  name: gaudi\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://gitlab.cern.ch/gaudi/Gaudi/-/archive/${{ tag }}/Gaudi-${{ tag }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: dd288f066e09237f2968a2390e80bef5580e0075896116f4d729b9b609bc25c8\n  patches:\n    # gaudi/Gaudi!1925 added getDefaultPluginPath() and wired it into\n    # loadPluginLibrary() but not Registry::initialize(), so in a Conda env\n    # with no GAUDI_PLUGIN_PATH / (DY)LD_LIBRARY_PATH the factory registry\n    # initialises empty and lookups (e.g. EvtDataSvc) fail. Pending upstream\n    # fix to be submitted as a follow-up to !1925.\n    - patches/0001-fix-scan-default-plugin-path-in-Registry-initialize.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  skip:\n    - win\n    # Skip macOS for now due to lack of upstream support\n    - osx\n    # conda-forge Python lacks gdbm support, so dbm.sqlite3 (Python 3.13+) is needed for confdb2\n    - match(python, \"<3.13\")\n  script:\n    - |\n      cmake ${CMAKE_ARGS} \\\n          -GNinja \\\n          -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \\\n          -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=$PREFIX \\\n          -DCMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS=ON \\\n          -DCMAKE_CXX_SCAN_FOR_MODULES=OFF \\\n          -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON \\\n          -DGAUDI_INSTALL_PYTHONDIR=$SP_DIR \\\n          -DGAUDI_DEFAULT_PLUGIN_PATH=$PREFIX/lib \\\n          -DPython_EXECUTABLE=$PYTHON \\\n          -DGAUDI_USE_DOXYGEN=OFF \\\n          -S $SRC_DIR \\\n          -B build\n      cmake --build build --parallel ${CPU_COUNT}\n    - which ps\n    # Exclude cmake.test_dummyGaudiDownstreamProject - requires vdt/ROOT\n    # development dependencies not available in test install environmet\n    # Exclude whiteboard.test_bug_cfhep114 - the reproducer requests a thread\n    # pool of 10 with cardinality 10 and consistently exceeds its 120s timeout\n    # under the oversubscription of a resource-constrained CI runner\n    # Gaudi tests are flaky on resource constrained environments to retry up to three times\n    - ctest --output-on-failure -E 'cmake\\.test_dummyGaudiDownstreamProject|whiteboard\\.test_bug_cfhep114' --repeat until-pass:3 -j${CPU_COUNT} --test-dir build\n    - cmake --install build\n    - root -l -b -q -e 'if (TClass::GetClass(\"DataObject\") == nullptr) { std::cerr << \"Failed to load DataObject\" << std::endl; return 1; } return 0;'\n\nrequirements:\n  run_exports:\n    - ${{ pin_subpackage(\"gaudi\", upper_bound=\"x.x.x\") }}\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - cmake\n    - ninja\n    # Gaudi invokes git at build/test time, and ps (procps-ng on linux) when\n    # running its test suite\n    - git\n    - if: linux\n      then: procps-ng\n  host:\n    # Gaudi's ctest suite drives pytest, so these are needed for the\n    # build-time test run\n    - python\n    - pytest\n    - pytest-cov\n    - coverage\n    - pyyaml\n    - networkx\n    - libboost-devel\n    - libboost-python-devel\n    - root_base\n    - root_cxx_standard\n    - tbb-devel\n    - zlib\n    - libuuid\n    - range-v3\n    - nlohmann_json\n    - fmt\n    - clhep\n    - xerces-c\n    - catch2\n    - ms-gsl\n    - aida\n    - heppdt\n  run:\n    - python\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - GaudiKernel\n      # Gaudi does not currently install Python package metadata, so pip_check\n      # would fail\n      pip_check: false\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - Gaudi\n  - script:\n      - Gaudi --help\n      - gaudirun.py\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://gitlab.cern.ch/gaudi/Gaudi\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: The Gaudi software framework for event data processing applications\n  description: |\n    Gaudi is a software framework used for building event data processing\n    applications in high-energy physics. It provides a component model,\n    an event data model, and interfaces for tools, services, and algorithms.\n    Originally developed at CERN for the LHCb experiment, it is now used\n    by multiple experiments including ATLAS and LHCb.\n  documentation: https://gaudi-framework.readthedocs.io/\n  repository: https://gitlab.cern.ch/gaudi/Gaudi\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - chrisburr\n",
